The bypass — manual thresholds
If you run thresh lb=X ub=Y before starting S2 (via the command box), _manual_thresholds_set = True and S2 skips the .hrs1 check entirely. The histogram plot shows a text label instead of bars. This is the only way to run S2 without S1 data.

In short: S2 uses S1's EMG amplitude histogram to set the background EMG window that must be satisfied before each trial is triggered. S1 characterizes what "quiet muscle" looks like for that subject; S2 uses those bounds to ensure the animal is at rest before each stimulus.


